  "limits": [
    "Only private mappings, optionally fixed/local/autoresrv; shared, autogrow, anyaddr and unknown flags remain EINVAL.",
    "AUTORESRV uses native UVM demand allocation; IRIX logical-swap accounting, exhaustion behavior and mlock interactions are not established.",
    "LOCAL requires one LWP and an unshared vmspace; sproc/share-group semantics are not implemented.",
    "Native page alignment, file permissions and protections remain authoritative; LP64 rounds 4096 bytes to 8192.",
    "Native /dev/zero permits mapping a write-only descriptor; original IRIX returns EACCES. Regular-file permission checks remain native.",
    "Native bad-protection/empty-map EINVAL and wrap ENOMEM differ from original IRIX.",
    "Only signed 32-bit file offsets are covered.",
    "Validated IRIX executables permit page zero; native executables retain the default guard, including after foreign-to-native exec."
  ]
